━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ErrorSets

` The errors a function raises are those its body raises and those of the calls in it that let
` errors through. A call can reach a callee before the callee's body is typed, so the end of a
` body may not know them all. It then leaves what it has here, and `settle` finishes the set
` once the bodies it waits on are typed. Functions on a cycle of such calls share the errors
` of the cycle.

+ held Table'HeldErrors
+ open List'InstanceId'ArenaBacking
+ unready Scratch'U32

_ entries Scratch'Outgoing
_ transforms Scratch'ErrorTransform
_ expanded Scratch'TypedSite
_ seen Scratch'U32
_ order Scratch'U32
_ low Scratch'U32
_ stacked Scratch'U32
_ stack Scratch'U32
_ reports Scratch'ErrorReport
_ reported Size = 0
_ round U32
_ counter U32
_ settled-through Size = 0
_ arena Arena
_ types Types
_ relations Relations
_ instances Instances
_ facts Facts
_ program Program

────────────────────
+ This
    - arena Arena
    - types Types
    - relations Relations
    - instances Instances
    - facts Facts
    - program Program

.. held = Table'HeldErrors(arena, 16)
.. open = List'InstanceId(arena)
.. unready = Scratch'U32(arena, 64)
.. entries = Scratch'Outgoing(arena, 64)
.. transforms = Scratch'ErrorTransform(arena, 16)
.. expanded = Scratch'TypedSite(arena, 64)
.. seen = Scratch'U32(arena, 16)
.. order = Scratch'U32(arena, 16)
.. low = Scratch'U32(arena, 16)
.. stacked = Scratch'U32(arena, 16)
.. stack = Scratch'U32(arena, 16)
.. reports = Scratch'ErrorReport(arena, 16)

────────────────────
+ do close-body
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - outgoing ImmutableArray'Outgoing'ArenaBacking
    - declared [ErrorTransform]
    - lacks-result Bool
    - unbuildable Bool

` Ends a body's errors. When no entry waits on a callee they are finished at once. Otherwise
` the entries and the transformers are kept until `settle` reaches the instance.
. waits = false
for entry in outgoing
    if entry.callee != U32.max
        waits = true
if !waits
    . mark = expanded.mark
    for entry in outgoing
        expanded.push(TypedSite(entry.type, entry.syntax))
    finish(instance, syntax, mark, lacks-result, unbuildable, false)
    expanded.rewind(mark)
    flush-reports()
    =
. entries-start U32 = entries.length as U32
for entry in outgoing
    entries.push(entry)
. transforms-start U32 = transforms.length as U32
for transform in declared
    transforms.push(transform)
. entry-count U32 = outgoing.length as U32
. transform-count U32 = declared.length as U32
. row = HeldErrors
    - instance
    - syntax
    - RowRange'Outgoing(entries-start, entry-count)
    - RowRange'ErrorTransform(transforms-start, transform-count)
    - lacks-result
    - unbuildable
. id U32 = held.length as U32
held.append(row)
seen.push(0)
order.push(0)
low.push(0)
stacked.push(0)
instances.signatures[instance].pending = id
open += instance

────────────────────
+ do retarget
    - next Program

program = next

────────────────────
+ do retire
    - retired [Bool]
    - dead InstanceId

for node in 0 .. < held.length
    . owner = held[node].instance
    if (owner as Size) < retired.length && retired[owner]
        held[node].instance = dead

────────────────────
+ do absorb
    - peer ErrorSets
    - ids PeerIds

` Takes in the errors another type pass over the program still held of the instances this pass
` takes from it (`PeerIds.owns`), which wait here on the bodies of their callees as they waited
` there.
for node in 0 .. < peer.held.length
    . row = peer.held[node] as HeldErrors
    if !ids.owns(row.instance) || peer.instances.signatures[row.instance].pending != node as U32
        continue
    . instance = ids.instance(row.instance)
    . entries-start U32 = entries.length as U32
    for offset in 0 .. < row.entries.count
        . entry = peer.entries[row.entries.start + offset]
        . type = ids.type(entry.type)
        . callee = if entry.callee == U32.max then U32.max else ids.instance(entry.callee)
        . call = if entry.call == U32.max then U32.max else ids.calls[entry.call]
        ?! Panic("Errors held by another type pass wait on a call it leaves")
            if entry.call != U32.max && call == U32.max
        entries.push(Outgoing(type, entry.syntax, callee, call, entry.transforms))
    . transforms-start U32 = transforms.length as U32
    for offset in 0 .. < row.transforms.count
        . transform = peer.transforms[row.transforms.start + offset]
        . source = ids.type(transform.source)
        . raised = ids.type(transform.raised)
        . fact = if transform.fact == U32.max then U32.max else ids.transforms[transform.fact]
        transforms.push(ErrorTransform(source, raised, transform.site, fact, transform.conditional))
    . id U32 = held.length as U32
    . entry-range = RowRange'Outgoing(entries-start, row.entries.count)
    . transform-range = RowRange'ErrorTransform(transforms-start, row.transforms.count)
    held.append
        - HeldErrors
            - instance
            - row.syntax
            - entry-range
            - transform-range
            - row.lacks-result
            - row.unbuildable
    seen.push(0)
    order.push(0)
    low.push(0)
    stacked.push(0)
    instances.signatures[instance].pending = id
    open += instance

────────────────────
+ do gather ScratchMark
    - root InstanceId

` Pushes onto `unready` every instance the root's errors wait on whose body is not typed yet,
` and gives the mark below them.
. base = unready.mark
if instances.errors-known(root)
    = base
. node = instances.signatures[root].pending
if node == U32.max
    if instances.rows[root].state == .instance-unstarted
        unready.push(root)
    = base
round += 1
reach(node)
= base

────────────────────
+ do settle
    - root InstanceId

` Finishes the errors of an instance and of every instance they wait on. The bodies they pass
` through are typed by now, apart from any still running further up the stack, which only a
` cycle reaches. Such a one counts as raising nothing so far, and is marked as read early.
. node = instances.signatures[root].pending
if node == U32.max
    if !instances.errors-known(root)
        instances.signatures[root].errors-read-early = true
    =
round += 1
counter = 0
visit(node)
flush-reports()

────────────────────
+ do settle-open

` Finishes every error set still held, once no body is left to type.
for position in settled-through .. < open.length
    settle(open[position])
settled-through = open.length

────────────────────
_ do reach
    - node U32

seen[node] = round
. row = held[node]
for offset in 0 .. < row.entries.count
    . entry = entries[row.entries.start + offset]
    if entry.callee == U32.max || instances.errors-known(entry.callee)
        continue
    . next = instances.signatures[entry.callee].pending
    if next != U32.max
        if seen[next] != round
            reach(next)
    else if instances.rows[entry.callee].state == .instance-unstarted
        unready.push(entry.callee)

────────────────────
_ do report
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - kind TypeDiagnosticKind
    - name Atom? = null
    - source TypeId = no-type

` Keeps a diagnostic until the search that found it is over. Recording one can check a class
` declaration, which can type a body and so start a search of its own.
reports.push(ErrorReport(instance, syntax, kind, name, source))

────────────────────
_ do flush-reports

` Records the diagnostics kept so far, in the order they were found.
while reported < reports.length
    . row = reports[reported]
    reported += 1
    . module = instances.rows[row.instance].module
    facts.record-diagnostic(row.instance, module, row.syntax, row.kind, row.name, row.source)
reports.rewind(0)
reported = 0

────────────────────
_ do visit
    - node U32

` One step of the search for the cycles among held instances. An instance whose calls lead
` back to nothing above it closes a group: itself, or itself and everything on a cycle with it.
seen[node] = round
order[node] = counter
low[node] = counter
counter += 1
. base = stack.mark
stack.push(node)
stacked[node] = 1
. loops = false
. row = held[node]
for offset in 0 .. < row.entries.count
    . entry = entries[row.entries.start + offset]
    if entry.callee == U32.max
        continue
    . next = instances.signatures[entry.callee].pending
    if next == U32.max
        if !instances.errors-known(entry.callee)
            instances.signatures[entry.callee].errors-read-early = true
        continue
    if next == node
        loops = true
    if seen[next] != round
        visit(next)
        low[node] = lower(low[node], low[next])
    else if stacked[next] == 1
        low[node] = lower(low[node], order[next])
if low[node] != order[node]
    =
. cyclic = loops || stack.length - base > 1
. changed = cyclic
while changed
    changed = false
    for position in base .. < stack.length
        if grow(stack[position])
            changed = true
for position in base .. < stack.length
    . member = stack[position]
    conclude(member, cyclic)
    stacked[member] = 0
stack.rewind(base)

────────────────────
_ lower U32
    - first U32
    - second U32

if first < second then first else second

────────────────────
_ do grow Bool
    - node U32

` Takes into an instance's inferred errors whatever its callees have gained, and says whether
` there was anything.
. row = held[node]
. signature = instances.signatures[row.instance]
if signature.error-state == .errors-stated
    = false
. mark = expanded.mark
expand(node, false)
. scratch = types.scratch
. types-mark = scratch.types.mark
for position in mark .. < expanded.length
    scratch.types.push(expanded[position].type)
expanded.rewind(mark)
order-errors(types, types-mark)
. count = scratch.types.length - types-mark
. generator = instances.rows[row.instance].is-generator
. known = if generator then step-count else signature.errors.count
    .. step-count = instances.rows[row.instance].step-errors.count
. grew = count != known
if grew && generator
    instances.set-step-errors(row.instance, scratch.types.since(types-mark))
else if grew
    instances.set-errors(row.instance, scratch.types.since(types-mark))
scratch.types.rewind(types-mark)
= grew

────────────────────
_ do conclude
    - node U32
    - cyclic Bool

. row = held[node]
. mark = expanded.mark
expand(node, true)
instances.signatures[row.instance].pending = U32.max
finish(row.instance, row.syntax, mark, row.lacks-result, row.unbuildable, cyclic)
expanded.rewind(mark)

────────────────────
_ do expand
    - node U32
    - marking Bool

` Lists the errors that leave a held instance in the order its body met them. A call stands for
` its callee's errors, each as the instance's transformers declared before the call let it
` out. With `marking`, a call whose callee raises is marked as propagating.
. row = held[node]
for offset in 0 .. < row.entries.count
    . entry = entries[row.entries.start + offset]
    if entry.callee == U32.max
        expanded.push(TypedSite(entry.type, entry.syntax))
        continue
    . callee = instances.signatures[entry.callee]
    if marking && callee.errors.count != 0 && entry.call != U32.max
        facts.calls[entry.call].propagates = true
    . declared [ErrorTransform]
    if callee.errors.count != 0
        for index in 0 .. < entry.transforms
            declared += transforms[row.transforms.start + index]
    for position in 0 .. < callee.errors.count
        . error = instances.signature-types[callee.errors.start + position]
        if entry.transforms == 0
            expanded.push(TypedSite(error, entry.syntax))
            continue
        . tried [U32]
        order-transforms(relations, error, declared, tried)
        . leaving [TypeId]
        transform-leaving
            - facts
            - types
            - row.instance
            - entry.syntax
            - error
            - declared
            - tried
            - leaving
            - marking
        for type in leaving
            expanded.push(TypedSite(type, entry.syntax))

────────────────────
_ do finish
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - mark ScratchMark
    - lacks-result Bool
    - unbuildable Bool
    - cyclic Bool

` Checks the errors above the mark, which leave an instance, against the errors it states, or
` makes them its error set when it states none. Where the instances keep those whose errors settle
` (`Instances.keeps-settled`), it joins them.
if lacks-result && expanded.length == mark
    report(instance, syntax, .non-void-return)
if unbuildable
    report(instance, syntax, .stated, program.store-atom("Type can not be constructed"))
. signature = instances.signatures[instance]
if signature.error-state == .errors-stated
    if instances.rows[instance].is-generator
        instances.move-step-errors(instance)
    . stated = if instances.rows[instance].is-generator then step-errors else signature.errors
        .. step-errors = instances.rows[instance].step-errors
    check-stated(instance, syntax, stated)
    check-leaving(instance, stated, mark)
    =
instances.signatures[instance].error-state = .errors-settled
if instances.keeps-settled
    instances.settled += instance
if expanded.length == mark
    =
report-rules(instance, mark)
. scratch = types.scratch
. types-mark = scratch.types.mark
for position in mark .. < expanded.length
    scratch.types.push(expanded[position].type)
order-errors(types, types-mark)
. generator = instances.rows[instance].is-generator
if cyclic || signature.errors-read-early
    . names = ""
    for error in scratch.types.since(types-mark)
        if names.length != 0
            names += ", "
        names += type-short-name(types, error)
    . kind = if generator then "generator" else "function"
    . message = "$names can leave recursive $kind ${function-name(instance)} before its errors "
    message ++= "are inferred; declare them with ?! $names, or catch them here"
    report(instance, expanded[mark].syntax, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
if generator
    instances.set-step-errors(instance, scratch.types.since(types-mark))
else
    instances.set-errors(instance, scratch.types.since(types-mark))
scratch.types.rewind(types-mark)

────────────────────
_ do report-rules
    - instance InstanceId
    - mark ScratchMark

` The reference makes functions of a local rule beside a match that calls itself before it
` knows what the function the rule is written in raises. So where that function states no
` errors, one that leaves the rule's arms, or the arms of a local rule they call, is
` reported as the reference reports it: at the first call of a rule in the rule's arms.
. row = instances.rows[instance]
. tree = program.modules[row.module].tree
. scratch = types.scratch
for local in facts.local-rules
    if local.instance != instance || !local.recursive || local.stream == no-type
        continue
    . reached [SyntaxId]
    reached += local.syntax
    . next = 0
    while next < reached.length
        for call in facts.rule-calls
            if call.instance == instance && call.from == reached[next] && unreached
                reached += call.to
            .. unreached = reached.find(call.to) == null
        next += 1
    . types-mark = scratch.types.mark
    for position in mark .. < expanded.length
        . site = expanded[position].syntax
        for rule in reached
            if site >= tree.subtree-start(rule) && site <= rule
                scratch.types.push(expanded[position].type)
                break
    order-errors(types, types-mark)
    . names = ""
    for error in scratch.types.since(types-mark)
        if names.length != 0
            names += ", "
        names += type-short-name(types, error)
    scratch.types.rewind(types-mark)
    if names.length == 0
        continue
    . first = local.syntax
    for node in tree.subtree-start(local.syntax) .. < local.syntax
        if tree.nodes[node] is .node-stream-call
            first = node
            break
    . message = "$names can leave recursive function $rule-text before its errors are "
        .. rule-text = rule-name(tree, local.syntax)
    message ++= "inferred; For a local '.. name ~' grammar, declare ?! $names on the enclosing "
    message ++= "'+ name ~ ...' function so generated pattern helpers inherit the result ABI."
    report(instance, first, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    =

────────────────────
_ do rule-name String
    - tree AST
    - rule SyntaxId

` The name a local rule is declared with.
do match? tree.nodes[rule]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        . named = declaration.left
        do match? tree.nodes[named]
            | .node-type-capture(row)
                named = row.id
        do match? tree.nodes[named]
            | .node-identifier(row)
                = row.name.text
= ""

────────────────────
_ do function-name String
    - instance InstanceId

. row = instances.rows[instance]
do match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        if fn.name
            = fn.name.text
= ""

────────────────────
_ do check-stated
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - stated RowRange'TypeId

` Only an error can be declared after `?!`: a panic ends its task instead of returning, and
` nothing else is raised at all.
for offset in 0 .. < stated.count
    . declared = instances.signature-types[stated.start + offset]
    if declared == invalid-type || declared == no-type
        continue
    types.complete(declared)
    . shown = type-short-name(types, declared)
    . message = ""
    if is-subtype(types, declared, types.panic-type)
        message = "$shown cannot be returned as a recoverable error; use ?! Panic(...) to end the task, "
        message ++= "or convert it explicitly."
    else if !is-subtype(types, declared, types.error-type)
        message = "$shown is not a recoverable error type; only subclasses of Error may appear "
        message ++= "after ?!."
    if message.length != 0
        report(instance, syntax, .stated, program.store-atom(message), declared)
        =

────────────────────
_ do check-leaving
    - instance InstanceId
    - stated RowRange'TypeId
    - mark ScratchMark

` Reports each error above the mark that leaves an instance and that no error it states takes.
` One takes an error that converts to it, as the reference compares them: a class below it, or
` one above it that a cast may find to be it, which panics where it is not, so the instance may.
for position in mark .. < expanded.length
    . error = expanded[position].type
    if error == invalid-type
        continue
    . accepted = false
    . casts = false
    for offset in 0 .. < stated.count
        . declared = instances.signature-types[stated.start + offset]
        if is-subtype(types, error, declared)
            accepted = true
        else if relation-legal(relations.compare(error, declared))
            casts = true
    if !accepted && casts
        instances.mark-casts-errors(instance)
        accepted = true
    if !accepted
        . name = program.store-atom(function-name(instance))
        . kind = if instances.rows[instance].is-generator then generator-kind else function-kind
            .. generator-kind = TypeDiagnosticKind.error-leaves-generator
            .. function-kind = TypeDiagnosticKind.error-leaves-function
        report(instance, expanded[position].syntax, kind, name, error)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ErrorTransform is Tuple

` A transformer a function declares: the error it takes, what it raises, the raise it is
` written with, its fact, and whether it tests a chain of earlier errors.

+ source TypeId
+ raised TypeId
+ site SyntaxId
+ fact U32
+ conditional Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ HeldErrors is Struct

` What the end of a body leaves when a callee's errors were not known: the entries on their way
` out, the function's transformers, and the two reports that wait on whether anything leaves.
+ instance InstanceId
+ syntax SyntaxId
+ entries RowRange'Outgoing
+ transforms RowRange'ErrorTransform
+ lacks-result Bool
+ unbuildable Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ do note-previous
    - facts Facts
    - types Types
    - instance InstanceId
    - site SyntaxId
    - error TypeId

` An error a transformer takes becomes the `previous` of the error raised in its place, which
` holds any error or none. That is a conversion at the transformer.
if error == invalid-type || error == no-type
    =
. held = types.optional-of(types.error-type)
facts.record-conversion(instance, site, side-cast-relation(error, held), .reason-assignment)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ caught-rank RelationRank?
    - relations Relations
    - error TypeId
    - source TypeId

` The rank at which a transformer declared for a source takes an error, or null when it does
` not take it.
relation.rank if relation.kind == .relation-same || relation.kind == .relation-up-cast

.. relation = relations.compare(error, source)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ do order-transforms
    - relations Relations
    - error TypeId
    - declared [ErrorTransform]
    - tried [U32]

` The transformers an error leaving a function is tried with, as TypeScript tries them: those
` whose source takes it, nearest first and then in the order declared, up to the first that
` tests no chain of earlier errors, which takes it whatever came before. Their places among
` `declared` are added to `tried`.
. ranks [RelationRank]
for index in 0 .. < declared.length
    . rank = caught-rank(relations, error, declared[index].source)
    if rank == null
        continue
    . place = tried.length
    while place > 0 && ranks[place - 1] > rank
        place -= 1
    tried.insert(index as U32, place)
    ranks.insert(rank, place)
for position in 0 .. < tried.length
    if !declared[tried[position]].conditional
        while tried.length > position + 1
            tried.pop()
        =

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ do transform-leaving
    - facts Facts
    - types Types
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - error TypeId
    - declared [ErrorTransform]
    - tried [U32]
    - leaving [TypeId]
    - noting Bool

` What an error leaving at a node leaves as through the transformers it is tried with: what
` each raises, and the error itself where each tests a chain of earlier errors. With `noting`
` each converts the error to the `previous` of what it raises, and the node keeps them.
. facts-tried [U32]
for place in tried
    . transform = declared[place]
    if noting
        note-previous(facts, types, instance, transform.site, error)
    leaving += transform.raised
    facts-tried += transform.fact
if tried.length == 0 || declared[tried[tried.length - 1]].conditional
    leaving += error
if noting && tried.length != 0
    facts.note-leave(instance, syntax, error, facts-tried)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ is-subtype Bool
    - types Types
    - from TypeId
    - to TypeId

to != invalid-type && from != invalid-type && in-base-chain(types, from, to)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ErrorReport is Tuple

+ instance InstanceId
+ syntax SyntaxId
+ kind TypeDiagnosticKind
+ name Atom?
+ source TypeId
